{"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Destination"}],"roleHeading":"Protocol","role":"symbol","title":"Destination","modules":[{"name":"Destinations"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Destination"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Destinations\/Destination.swift#L27","fileName":"Destination.swift"},"externalID":"s:12Destinations11DestinationP","symbolKind":"protocol"},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Destinations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/ConsoleDestination","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InvalidCapacity"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Destinations"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/destinations\/destination"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Destination"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","text":"Sendable"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:bufferDropReporter:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" gives each destination its batches in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order the events were tracked, one at a time: the next batch comes once "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returns. Batches that arrive meanwhile wait in a buffer of the destination’s own, which drops"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its oldest batch when full, so a destination that falls behind doesn’t hold up the others."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The delivery reports each batch dropped. Once the destination has caught up, it gets the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dropped batch’s records that a store keeps, read back from the store, after the newer batches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it received meanwhile; those kept in memory only are lost."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" should return as soon as the batch is somewhere it won’t be lost, and honour"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cancellation: a delivery waits for it before it completes, and cancels it when the delivery is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cancelled. Until it returns, this destination’s later batches wait in its buffer. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination handles its own errors (a failed upload, say); the delivery has none to receive."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When a tracker keeps its records in a store, returning from ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is what tells the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store a batch arrived: once every destination has returned for it, uncancelled, the store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"forgets those records. A destination that buffers or retries should return only once the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batch is somewhere it won’t be lost; a record whose ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord.isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is set may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"have reached it in an earlier run.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What a destination receives is narrowed by modifiers rather than by code of its own:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/accepting(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the consent categories it serves, "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/redactingSensitiveValues()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/droppingCallSite()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". A destination given none receives every record as tracked."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Where a delivery sends events: a plain sink that records the batches it receives.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/accepting(_:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/droppingCallSite()","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/enriched(by:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/redactingSensitiveValues()"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Inherits From","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Destinations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"inheritsFrom","kind":"relationships"},{"title":"C